From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtio_balloon: drain the full OOM deflate budget across batches

0005 raises VIRTIO_BALLOON_OOM_NR_PAGES to 32768 (128 MiB), but a single
leak_balloon() call moves at most VIRTIO_BALLOON_ARRAY_PFNS_MAX pfns
per tell_host() round-trip (32 MiB with the 8192 batch) - the rest of
the budget was silently discarded, so an OOM event still freed only
one batch.

Loop leak_balloon() until the 128 MiB budget is freed or no progress
is made (fully-pinned balloon), updating the actual size after. A
spiking guest now gets up to 4x32 MiB back per OOM event instead of
OOM-killing in a loop while the host re-inflates.

No behaviour change when the balloon is empty (first leak returns 0)
or the host does not balloon.

Signed-off-by: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
---
 drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
index 123456789024..123456789025 100644
--- a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
+++ b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
@@ -914,8 +914,22 @@
 						 struct virtio_balloon, oom_nb);
 	unsigned long *freed = parm;
 
-	*freed += leak_balloon(vb, VIRTIO_BALLOON_OOM_NR_PAGES) /
-		  VIRTIO_BALLOON_PAGES_PER_PAGE;
+	unsigned long remaining = VIRTIO_BALLOON_OOM_NR_PAGES;
+	unsigned long got;
+
+	/*
+	 * Maximum survival: drain up to OOM_NR_PAGES across multiple
+	 * tell_host() batches (one leak_balloon() moves at most
+	 * ARRAY_PFNS_MAX). Stop on no progress so a fully-pinned
+	 * balloon cannot livelock OOM handling.
+	 */
+	while (remaining) {
+		got = leak_balloon(vb, remaining);
+		if (!got)
+			break;
+		*freed += got / VIRTIO_BALLOON_PAGES_PER_PAGE;
+		remaining -= got;
+	}
 	update_balloon_size(vb);
 
 	return NOTIFY_OK;
-- 
2.47.0
